WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.820
We can only imagine just how long it would
take to plow through all of Netflix’s many

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:08.460
movies, documentaries, and TV shows; months,
maybe, or even years.

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:12.940
With so many titles available to subscribers,
it can be easy to get a little overwhelmed

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.280
by everything the streaming service has to
offer.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.280
Luckily, we’ve compiled this list of a few
of Netflix’s finest hidden gems: the perfect

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:23.480
go-tos next time you find yourself at a loss
for what to watch.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:25.920
Beyond Skyline

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.100
B-movies usually tend to get a fairly bad
rap, thanks to their lower-than-average budgets,

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:35.609
questionable performances, and poor scripts,
and, let's be honest, Beyond Skyline fits

00:00:35.609 --> 00:00:38.020
snugly into pretty much all of those categories.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.010
The basic plot is this: Aliens invade Earth
using a bunch of high-tech blue lights which

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:46.900
turn people into zombies, allowing said aliens
to harvest their brains.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.690
Enter Frank Grillo as Mark, an alcoholic cop
whose principal method for dealing with the

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:55.100
aliens can be largely summed up as: ‘punching
them until they go away’.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:01:00.320
So, yes, it sounds like your typical B-movie
dud, but Beyond Skyline is clearly a labor

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:00.820
of love.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.940
The movie’s attention to detail betrays
a passion on the part of the filmmakers that

00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:08.610
you’d struggle to even find in many of today’s
big-budget blockbusters.

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:09.980
Also, it's a lot of fun.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:12.900
If you’ve got a soft spot for genre movies,
you’ll have a blast.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:20.820
The Boy

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:25.420
On the surface, The Boy appears to be your
average, run-of-the-mill horror movie: it’s

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:29.490
about a young American nanny who takes a job
caring for the son of an elderly couple in

00:01:29.490 --> 00:01:30.600
the English countryside.

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:34.920
She thinks they’re playing a joke when she
discovers that their son is actually a porcelain

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.220
doll named Brahms, but soon begins to suspect
that there's more to the doll than meets the

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:39.720
eye.

00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:44.420
Underneath that pretty thin premise, however,
is a movie which is totally willing to embrace

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:45.380
its own silliness.

00:01:45.749 --> 00:01:49.860
It manages to spend just enough time poking
fun at itself to remain charming, all the

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.560
while delivering a satisfyingly creepy story
and a solid twist ending.

00:01:55.160 --> 00:01:55.660
The Gift

00:01:56.280 --> 00:02:01.460
This 2015 horror-thriller, written, directed
by and starring Joel Edgerton, delivers on

00:02:01.479 --> 00:02:05.659
all fronts, making for a tense, dramatic stalker
flick that’s bound to keep you guessing

00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:06.160
to the end.

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:11.060
Edgerton stars as Gordo, a mysterious loner
who runs into an old friend from high school.

00:02:11.300 --> 00:02:15.330
Although Gordo might seem like your typical
outcast at first, his sinister intentions

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.520
slowly become clear.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:20.660
Nothing groundbreaking here, then, but The
Gift benefits from a cast of well-written

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:23.400
characters and a captivating approach to morality.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:27.660
Before long, you’ll find yourself questioning
just who the movie’s real villain really

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:28.160
is.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:30.060
The Tiger Hunter

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:34.940
Equal parts cheesy and sweet, The Tiger Hunter
is the story of an Indian immigrant in the

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:39.920
late '70s who comes to America in search of
a job, only to find something even better:

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:40.640
a purpose.

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:45.260
It's a total feel-good movie from start to
finish, the kind of gem best saved as an antidote

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.580
to some terrifying horror movie, a downbeat
drama, or anything starring Sean Penn.

00:02:49.700 --> 00:02:52.400
Think of it as Prozac, but with better cinematography.

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:58.720
It’s not a movie that’s going to change
the world anytime soon, but you can’t say

00:02:58.720 --> 00:02:59.240
it’s not lovely.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:01.200
And sometimes that’s enough.

00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:03.420
Pandora

00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:07.700
It’s a story you’ll probably feel like
you’ve heard before: a nuclear reactor goes

00:03:07.700 --> 00:03:12.980
haywire after a devastating earthquake, endangering
the citizens of a small South Korean town.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:17.340
As various government officials try to escape
the blame, the ordinary folk do their best

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.360
to avoid the cataclysmic destruction of the
reactor itself.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:21.840
So far, so bland, right?

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:26.160
Well, stick around, because towards the end
Pandora suddenly transforms into something

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:30.430
so beautiful and touching that you can't help
but wonder if Netflix's autoplay switched

00:03:30.430 --> 00:03:31.840
movies without you noticing.

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:35.720
The rest of Pandora is decent enough, but
that ending is one for the ages.

00:03:37.140 --> 00:03:37.860
The Perfect Host

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:42.560
David Hyde Pierce, best known for playing
Niles on Frasier, here takes on a role as

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:47.020
a high-strung gentleman who unknowingly accepts
a criminal into his home on the eve of a dinner

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:47.520
party.

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:52.220
Before long, the script is flipped, and a
whole slew of secrets about both men are subsequently

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:52.720
revealed.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:57.660
Clayne Crawford co-stars as the hapless criminal
John Taylor, and both he and Pierce work hard

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:00.460
to turn what could have been a flat movie
into a total thrill ride.

00:04:00.790 --> 00:04:04.960
The plot is riddled with twists, each building
on the other until the movie reaches a final

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:05.720
fever pitch.

00:04:06.100 --> 00:04:08.180
We can't say much more without risking spoilers.

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.700
Queue it up, and let it rip.

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:11.820
Boys in the Trees

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:16.850
The events of this criminally-underrated Australian
flick play out over the course of one Halloween

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:21.570
night, as two former friends, one popular,
the other a social outcast, reunite for a

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:25.360
long walk home, filled with stories about
their childhood and their lost friendship.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:31.070
As each story is told, Boys in the Trees further
embraces its macabre, fairy tale tone, reinforced

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:35.570
by an array of colorful visuals and anchored
by the real-life social conflicts each character

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:37.120
faces in their day-to-day life.

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:42.200
First-time writer/director Nicholas Verso
balances those two sides of the story perfectly,

00:04:42.200 --> 00:04:45.880
never allowing the fantasy to cheapen the
reality of the film or vice versa.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:49.780
It's both stunningly visceral and chock-full
of childhood wonder.

00:04:49.780 --> 00:04:50.870
A rare gem indeed.

